# .allowed-domains — domains to whitelist on container startup
#
# Copy this file to your project root as .allowed-domains and customize.
# One domain per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# These domains are loaded automatically when the container starts.
# In --locked mode, these are the ONLY domains allowed (besides Anthropic API).
# In default mode, you can also approve additional domains at runtime.
#
# To remove a domain you don't need, delete or comment out the line.

# --- Package registries ---
registry.npmjs.org
deb.debian.org

# --- Code hosting ---
github.com
api.github.com

# --- VS Code services (only needed for VS Code Dev Container approach) ---
marketplace.visualstudio.com
vscode.blob.core.windows.net
update.code.visualstudio.com
